"""The turn: a question answered by a task in this worker, not by the request that asked it.

A persona can take a minute over a long answer, so a refresh, a locked phone
or a closed tab must not end it (`app-factory docs/design/agent-console.md`
§The turn). The asking request streams the turn while it listens; the task
goes on without it, and the answer lands in the agent's transcript either way.

The stream opens with this slice's own `system`/`init` naming the
conversation before the agent starts, so a stop has an address from the
first second. For a persona that chats with collections the turn then starts
the persona and retrieves at once, since the CLI's start-up and the library's
search each take a second or so: it searches the collections in scope for the
question as the person may read them, sends the passages as a `citations`
frame the moment they arrive, records them on the turn, and hands the persona
the question with the passages appended. A library that cannot be read ends
the turn with one error frame, the persona never asked and nothing charged.
The agent's own `init` follows with the same address as this slice's: its
session id is the agent's to keep (`conversations.claim`), never the page's.
Everything else is the agent's event, verbatim, through the app's
`agent_event` hook; a document version the agent wrote (`artefact`) is also
recorded on the turn, so a reopened conversation offers it again.

An edited question (`edit`) replaces the question at that place and every
turn after it, once the agent has taken it: its transcript taken back to the
answer before it, or, with none, a new session started and the old one
forgotten. Until then the question waits at the end of the record, and a
turn that ends before the agent takes it leaves the conversation as it was.

A stop is a row flag, so it reaches the turn from any worker: the task reads
it every second and closes the agent, which kills the local CLI.
"""

import asyncio
import contextlib
import functools
import logging
import math
import time
import uuid
from collections.abc import AsyncIterator, Awaitable, Callable
from dataclasses import dataclass
from pathlib import Path
